INT. RIDESHARE CAR - NIGHT

2 AM. Rain. A hatchback, wipers going. GWEN, bride-to-be, in a wedding dress, sits in back. Next to her, RICKY, her ex. Up front, TASHA drives. Beside her, BOB, a stranger with a trombone case.

TASHA
So to confirm. Four people. One dress. Zero explanations.

GWEN
He's not with me.

RICKY
I'm totally with her.

GWEN
He's not WITH me with me.

Silence.

Bob. Trombone. Nothing.

BOB
I got in the wrong car.

TASHA
You got in the right car. You got in the wrong, uh, situation.

Her phone. Dead.

GWEN
Does anyone have a charger

TASHA
Glovebox. Next to my dignity.

He opens it. Empty. Rain.

RICKY
Gwen, the groom is at the church. Everyone is at the church. Why are we in a Honda?

GWEN
Because I ran. Okay? I ran. In heels.

BOB
(raising trombone case)
For what it's worth, I think you look fantastic.

Beat. All three turn to him.

TASHA
Sir, you're not even supposed to be here.

BOB
I'm just saying. Great dress.

She laughs, then cries, then laughs. He hands her a napkin from the case. Why does he have napkins in a trombone case. Nobody asks.

Tasha stops the car. Church. Lights on. Doors open. The groom, tiny in the distance, waving.

RICKY
Oh no.

GWEN
Oh no.

TASHA
Five stars everybody. Thats the best ride I ever had.
